# Architecture

This project is a client-side SPA.

Do not introduce SSR or server-rendered pages unless explicitly requested.

---

# Navigation

Preserve native browser behavior.

For normal page navigation, use semantic links (`<Link>` or `<a>`).

Do not use imperative navigation (`navigate()`) where a link is appropriate.

Imperative navigation is only acceptable after completing an action such as login, logout, form submission, or deletion.

---

# URL Design

Each page must have its own stable URL.

State that users may want to refresh, bookmark, share, or revisit should be represented in the URL rather than only in client-side state.

---

# Browser Behavior

Do not implement custom behavior that breaks standard browser features such as:

- Back / Forward
- Refresh
- Ctrl + Click
- Middle-click
- Open in new tab
- Copy link

When multiple implementations are possible, prefer the one that preserves native browser behavior.